+# Cycles After Hours
+
+Cycles After Hours is a custom Blender/Cycles build focused on adding useful
+rendering and viewport features that are not currently available in stock Cycles.
+It is an independent project, not an official Blender Foundation product.
+
+## Features
+
+### Feature 001 — Viewport Motion Blur
+
+Adds true Cycles motion blur to the Cycles rendered viewport. See the
+[feature index](FEATURES.md), [feature guide](docs/features/viewport-motion-blur/README.md),
+and [changelog](CHANGELOG.md).
+
+More features may be added over time. All completed features are intended to
+coexist in the same Cycles After Hours executable. Develop from the stable
+codebase, test the new work, and rerun every existing feature's regressions
+against that same executable before integration.
+
+## Repository organization
+
+This directory contains project-specific documentation, tests, a sample scene,
+and a regression runner. Blender/Cycles implementation stays in the standard
+upstream source layout. The upstream [README](../README.md), [license](../COPYING),
+build instructions and contribution information remain authoritative for Blender.
+No renderer code or build-system file was changed for this organizational migration.
+
+- `docs/features/viewport-motion-blur/`: behavior, implementation map and testing.
+- `tests/viewport-motion-blur/scripts/`: existing regression scenarios and checkers.
+- `tests/viewport-motion-blur/scenes/`: reusable saved test scene.
+- `tools/run_regressions.py`: runs all current feature regressions with one executable.
+
+See [testing instructions](docs/features/viewport-motion-blur/testing.md).
+Results belong outside the source tree, in a new directory for every run.
+Future builds may use `C:\blender-git\cycles-after-hours-builds\<build-name>`;
+the supported Blender build process still applies. This migration creates no build.
+
+## History and branch policy
+
+The original Feature 001 release remains `viewport-motion-blur-v0.1.1` at
+`a500f2f7eb7e50c40283f4da7e1a21a4761b0115`, based on Blender 5.2.2 LTS.
+Historical tags, builds, evidence and backups keep their original names.
+See [provenance and preservation](docs/features/viewport-motion-blur/provenance.md).
+
+The current branch remains `cycles-viewport-motion-blur`. After this migration is
+reviewed, a stable `cycles-after-hours` integration branch with short-lived
+`feature/<name>` branches would express the long-term project model. Keep upstream
+tracking separate and preserve release tags. A future repository slug of
+`cycles-after-hours` is recommended; no branch, remote or repository is renamed here.
