+# Feature 001 — implementation map
+
+The implementation is preserved at historical commit
+`a500f2f7eb7e50c40283f4da7e1a21a4761b0115`. These are all implementation files
+changed relative to Blender release commit `d13f752e3b9`. Paths are relative to the
+repository root. None is moved or edited by the Cycles After Hours migration.
+
+| File | Responsibility |
+| --- | --- |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/addon/properties.py` | Viewport property and existing object motion-property update callbacks. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/addon/ui.py` | One checkbox in the existing Motion Blur panel. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/camera.cpp` | Viewport shutter/camera sampling and preserving sampled camera state across redraws. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/object.cpp` | Existing object transform/deformation sampling enabled for the viewport path; scoped evaluated-time restoration. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/session.cpp` | Trigger motion synchronization during viewport scene updates. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/sync.cpp` | Motion requirements and resynchronization of motion geometry. |
+| `intern/cycles/blender/sync.h` | Synchronization state declarations. |
+| `intern/cycles/scene/object.cpp` | Recompute packed motion transforms when buffer allocation or object offsets change. |
+| `intern/cycles/scene/scene.cpp` | Upload pending camera shutter lookup-table data during resolution updates. |
+| `source/blender/depsgraph/intern/depsgraph_eval.cc` | Preserve fractional evaluation time. |
+| `source/blender/depsgraph/intern/eval/deg_eval_copy_on_write.cc` | Preserve scene frame/subframe when copying evaluated state. |
+
+## Reused motion pipeline
+
+The new property gates viewport motion requirements together with existing scene and
+view-layer controls. Final-render selection remains independent of the new property.
+Existing object/camera shutter times, transform and deformation arrays, motion BVH
+and Cycles kernels perform the rendering. There is no alternate viewport blur algorithm.
+
+The existing per-object sampling helper supplies the motion count (for example,
+3 transform samples at Motion Steps 1 and 17 at Motion Steps 4), subject to existing
+geometry and velocity-cache behavior. The tests check two and sixteen distinct
+nonzero relative sample times respectively; the center sample accounts for the
+remaining entry. Existing object/deformation toggles remain authoritative.
+
+Viewport sampling temporarily evaluates the depsgraph with writeback disabled and
+restores evaluation time and active state. It does not drive the original scene
+timeline through shutter times. Motion geometry refresh occurs on requested scene
+synchronization, not on every render sample.
+
+## Preserved fixes
+
+Progressive viewport resolution changes can leave shutter lookup-table data pending.
+Uploading it before rendering prevents the repeated reset loop documented in the
+accumulation investigation. The log checker verifies forward sample progress after
+settling, rather than assuming identical screenshots imply convergence.
+
+Changing object Motion Steps can reallocate the packed transform buffer or move an
+unchanged object's offset. All affected decomposed transforms must be regenerated,
+including when the total size stays constant. The v0.1.1 fix addresses both cases;
+the multi-object regression checks that unrelated objects remain intact.
+
+Device backends, denoising implementation and final-render kernels were not replaced.
+The shared synchronization path is exercised by CPU tests; GPU behavior still needs
+backend-specific manual verification. See [testing](testing.md) for the actual scope.
