+# Feature 001 — regression testing
+
+## Run the suite
+
+Use a Python 3.11+ interpreter (the verified Blender's bundled Python works) and
+one explicit Blender executable. On Windows an interactive desktop is required:
+these are scripted GUI viewport tests as well as background render checks.
+The runner requests hidden process startup; Blender may show its render windows.
+The saved scene follows Blender's existing Git LFS rules. Ensure Git LFS has
+materialized `tests/viewport-motion-blur/scenes/motion-test.blend` before running;
+the runner's scene-load check rejects a missing or unresolved fixture.
+
+```powershell
+& 'C:\blender-git\build\_windows\_x64\_vc17\_Release\_v0.1.1\_fresh\bin\Release\5.2\python\bin\python.exe' -B `
+  'C:\blender-git\blender\cycles_after_hours\tools\run_regressions.py' `
+  --blender 'C:\blender-git\build\_windows\_x64\_vc17\_Release\_v0.1.1\_fresh\bin\Release\blender.exe' `
+  --output-root 'C:\blender-git\cycles-after-hours-migration-verification\run-01'
+```
+
+Choose a **new output directory** on each run; the runner refuses existing paths.
+The example above is the migration run and must not be reused. Keep results outside
+source and build directories, for example under
+`C:\blender-git\cycles-after-hours-regression-results\<unique-run-name>`.
+No build, package, Git mutation or source diagnostic is part of the runner.
+
+The runner sets `CAH_TEST_OUTPUT_ROOT` for its child processes. Five migrated scripts
+use that required environment variable instead of the old absolute result roots.
+Existing `--case=...` names still select subdirectories within Motion Steps and
+accumulation results. For direct invocation, explicitly set the variable to a new
+result root first. The accumulation checker still takes its log path as an argument.
+
+## Existing scenarios and assertions
+
+| Scripts | Coverage |
+| --- | --- |
+| `viewport-motion-test.py` (background) | Default checkbox, five F12 off/on pairs, original pixel baseline, frame preservation; regenerates a scene under results. |
+| `viewport-motion-test.py` (GUI), `viewport-motion-metrics.py` | 26 stages: transform, rotation, scale, deformation, Geometry Nodes, animated camera, navigation, drivers, frame/subframe and shutter behavior. Image extent, settled hashes and time assertions. |
+| Same GUI script with `--rolling` | 5 stages: rolling shutter, duration, denoising and animated-object deletion; checked with viewport metrics. |
+| `motion-steps-stress.py --extended`, `motion-steps-metrics.py --require-pass` | 74 stages: repeated slow/rapid Motion Steps edits, unrelated-object integrity, equal-size buffer layout swaps, object/deformation toggles, camera/object, shutter, frame/subframe, navigation and duplication/deletion. |
+| `accumulation-test.py`, `accumulation-check.py --require-pass` | 14 stages, six captures each: continued full-resolution samples after settling, no repeated resets, motion-time counts for low/high steps and no motion samples for Object Use Motion Blur off. |
+| Same accumulation scripts with `--camera --end --denoise --diagnose` | 3 stages combining animated camera/object motion, END shutter and viewport denoising. |
+
+The runner also opens the imported scene without saving it, verifies its enabled
+viewport property and frame, records executable/script hashes and version, checks
+GUI error files and exact completion counts, and stops on the first failure.
+It writes `summary.json`, logs, screenshots, scene and metrics under the new root.
+Original test scenarios and assertions were retained; only result-path setup changed.
+
+The F12 baseline is an existing image hash and checkbox off/on comparison, not a new
+comparison against a separate stock-Blender executable. All automated renders select
+CPU. OpenImageDenoise coverage does not establish GPU device/backend coverage.
+See the [manual checklist and limitations](README.md#limits-and-manual-checks).
+
+## Interpreting failures
+
+Check the failing log, `summary.json`, and any `*error.txt` first. Missing assets,
+incorrect script paths or output paths are tooling issues. Preserve failed evidence.
+Do not relax image, timing or motion assertions to obtain a pass. A renderer failure
+requires a separate development investigation; frozen release source is not patched
+as part of an organizational migration.
+
+Future feature suites should be added to the same runner and use its one executable
+argument, so integration runs exercise every completed feature together.
